dialogue trust_barbarian_3
title: Tithe day
trigger: Trust barbarian level=3
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  Past the wagons, out where the firelight thins, the Barbarian stands with a wooden tithe token turning over and over in one hand.
  -> asked

node asked hero
  I said I'd tell you about the red some night. This is the night, if you'll walk a bit.
  -> brother

node brother hero
  My brother was the gentle one. Fed the goats, sang to them. Then a tithe year came when the Choir's collectors wanted more than their share, and they took it out of him.
  -> grey

node grey hero
  He came back grey. Sat by the door all winter and didn't know my name. The collector laughed about it at the well. That's when the red came. I broke his arm in two places, and I ran for the moors before they could hang me.
  -> answer

node answer commander
  The token stops turning. The Barbarian doesn't look up.
  * The Choir will answer for him. I'll see to it. -> avenge
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag barbarian:tithe_avenge
  * Is he still alive? Then we can still go back for him. -> home
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag barbarian:tithe_home
  * You can't carry that into every fight. One day it'll carry you instead. -> warned
    do: AddTrust $with -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian:tithe_warned
  * Is that why the word is Saltmoss? -> word
    if: FlagSet barbarian:rage_word
    do: AddTrust $with 7
    do: SetFlag barbarian:tithe_word

node avenge hero
  Aye. And when they do, I'd like to be standing close enough to watch.
  -> where

node home hero
  Alive. Sitting by a door in Saltmoss, last I heard. I've never once let myself think "go back". You say it like it's a road.
  -> where

node warned hero
  You think I don't know that? It's carried me since I was fifteen. It's the only thing that ever has.
  -> where

node word hero
  You remembered. Aye. Every time you shout it I see that door, and him sitting in it. It's why I come back.
  -> where

node where hero
  You're from before, Commander. Before the Choir, before the tithe. So tell me. Where does it go, what they take?
  -> truth

node truth commander
  The old memory gives nothing back. Only the shape of a question the Commander once asked too.
  * I don't remember. I won't pretend I do. -> honest
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag barbarian:asked_honest
  * Wherever it goes, we'll follow it there. -> follow
    do: AddTrust $with 4
    do: SetFlag barbarian:asked_follow
  * It doesn't matter where it goes. Only who takes it. -> who
    do: AddTrust $with -2
    do: SetFlag barbarian:asked_who

node honest hero
  Good. I've had enough of people who knew everything. The collectors knew everything.
  -> token

node follow hero
  Then I'll walk point. Someone ought to see it first.
  -> token

node who hero
  It matters to me, Commander. Some of him's in it.
  -> token

node token hero
  This was his. The token they gave him for paying. Tells you how much of him they took, if you can read the marks. I never could bring myself to learn.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Barbarian closes a fist around the token and walks back toward the fire, slower than before.
